* Behavioral enhancement-mode (p-GaN gate) GaN HEMT model for ngspice
* Illustrative, simplified model: NOT calibrated to a real device and NOT a
* production compact model (see README for limitations).
*
* Channel : smooth subthreshold-to-strong-inversion gate drive, velocity-
*           saturation-limited drain current, symmetric (reverse conduction)
* Charges : Cgs constant; Cgd, Cds voltage dependent via analytic charges
* Parasitics: series Rg, Rd (access region), Rs

* smooth gate overdrive (softplus), floor avoids divide-by-zero
.func gtv(vg,vth,nv) {nv*ln(1+exp((vg-vth)/nv))+1e-12}

* drain current for vd >= 0
.func chan(vg,vd,k,vth,nv,vc) {k*gtv(vg,vth,nv)*vd/sqrt(1+pow(vd*(gtv(vg,vth,nv)+vc)/(gtv(vg,vth,nv)*vc),2))}

* smooth max(v,0): avoids a derivative kink (and wrong small-signal C) at v = 0
.func sp(v) {0.5*(v+sqrt(v*v+1e-6))}

* charge of a depletion-type capacitance C(v) = c0/(1+v/vj)^m for v >= 0
.func qjp(v,c0,vj,m) {c0*vj/(1-m)*(pow(1+sp(v)/vj,1-m)-1)}

* same, extended linearly with C = c0 for v < 0
.func qje(v,c0,vj,m) {qjp(v,c0,vj,m)+c0*(v-sp(v))}

.subckt gan_hemt_beh d g s
+ params: K=30 VTH=1.4 NV=0.039 VC=3 RDRIFT=3m RSRC=0.5m RGATE=0.6
+         CGS=700p CGD0=300p VJG=0.5 MG=0.95 CDS0=3000p VJD=1.5 MD=0.5

RG g gi {RGATE}
RD d di {RDRIFT}
RS s si {RSRC}

* channel current (symmetric: swap drain/source roles when vds < 0)
BCH di si I = V(di,si)>=0 ? chan(V(gi,si),V(di,si),K,VTH,NV,VC) : -chan(V(gi,di),-V(di,si),K,VTH,NV,VC)

* capacitances
CGSX gi si {CGS}
CGDX di gi q = qje(V(di,gi),CGD0,VJG,MG)
CDSX di si q = qjp(V(di,si),CDS0,VJD,MD) - qjp(-V(di,si),CDS0,VJD,MD)

* tiny leakage for numerical stability
RLK di si 1G
.ends gan_hemt_beh
